---
import Main from "../../layouts/Main.astro";
import PageHeader from "../../components/PageHeader.astro";
---

<Main
  title="The District - SyncID Labs"
  description="The HI-Tech Innovation District: a dense, mixed-use district on 89 acres in Markham, with labs, greenhouses, a sovereign-compute test-bed, and a battery-recycling facility."
  lang="en"
  activePath="/district"
>
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="The district"
    title="The HI-Tech Innovation District."
    lead="A dense, mixed-use, arcology-like district on 89 acres in Markham. On-site innovator residency, labs, greenhouses, a sovereign-compute test-bed, and a battery-recycling facility."
  />

  <section class="border-b border-hairline">
    <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-7xl gap-10 px-6 py-20 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:px-10">
      <div class="lg:col-span-3">
        <p class="eyebrow text-graphite/60">The five-year proof</p>
      </div>
      <div class="lg:col-span-9">
        <p class="max-w-3xl text-2xl leading-snug text-ink">
          In five years this land will hold working labs, greenhouses, a sovereign-compute
          test-bed, and a battery-recycling facility. Concrete, revenue-generating, and visible.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-7xl gap-10 px-6 py-20 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:px-10">
      <div class="lg:col-span-3">
        <p class="eyebrow text-graphite/60">Why a district, not a park</p>
      </div>
      <div class="lg:col-span-9">
        <p class="max-w-3xl text-2xl leading-snug text-ink">
          We build the founder pipeline first, then the buildings. A district earns its density
          from the people and ventures inside it, not from the real estate.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Main>
